  "source_text": "Hecks.bluebook \"Relay\" do\n  # A CORPUS-OWNED DOMAIN (docs/semantics/bluebook-semantics.md, C10.3).\n  # No example domain declares two saga legs on the SAME event with\n  # different `from:` states, so the clause that decides which leg\n  # answers could not be pinned against any of them. This domain exists\n  # for exactly that shape and nothing else: one parcel, scanned twice —\n  # the first scan picks it up, the second hands it over and dispatches\n  # the delivery. Under first-match-by-event-name (the pre-C10.3\n  # reading) the second scan would find the first leg again, refuse it\n  # as \"in picked_up, not posted\", and the parcel would never be\n  # delivered.\n  vision \"A parcel is posted, scanned along the way, and delivered when its last scan lands.\"\n  core\n\n  aggregate \"Parcel\" do\n    identified_by :tag\n\n    attribute :tag, Tag\n\n    value_object \"Tag\", String\n\n    lifecycle :status, default: \"posted\" do\n      transition \"Scan\"    => \"in_transit\", from: [\"posted\", \"in_transit\"]\n      transition \"Deliver\" => \"delivered\",  from: \"in_transit\"\n    end\n\n    command \"Post\" do\n      goal \"Hand a parcel to the relay\"\n      attribute :tag, Tag\n      emits \"ParcelPosted\"\n    end\n\n    command \"Scan\" do\n      goal \"Record the parcel passing a hand-over point\"\n      reference_to Parcel\n      emits \"ParcelScanned\"\n    end\n\n    command \"Deliver\" do\n      goal \"Mark the parcel delivered once its last scan lands\"\n      reference_to Parcel\n      emits \"ParcelDelivered\"\n    end\n  end\n\n  process_manager \"Delivery\" do\n    correlates_by :\"tag.value\"\n    starts_on \"ParcelPosted\"\n    ends_on   \"ParcelDelivered\"\n\n    # TWO LEGS, ONE EVENT — selected by (event, current state), C10.3.\n    transition \"ParcelScanned\" => \"picked_up\",   from: \"posted\"\n    transition \"ParcelScanned\" => \"handed_over\", from: \"picked_up\" do\n      dispatch Parcel::Deliver, with: { parcel: :tag }\n    end\n  end\nend\n"
}